From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukas Rieger <lukas@0x53a.dev>
Date: Thu, 13 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: Enable PMIC RTC write support

The Qualcomm PMIC RTC (qcom,qpnp-rtc on PM660) is set to read-only by
default in the device tree (qcom,qpnp-rtc-write = <0>). This causes the
kernel driver to register with qpnp_rtc_ro_ops which has no set_time
callback, making hwclock -w fail with EINVAL.

The hardware fully supports RTC writes — the driver has the code path
(qpnp_rtc_set_time writes epoch seconds to SPMI registers 0x6040-0x6043).
Setting qpnp-rtc-write to 1 makes the driver use qpnp_rtc_rw_ops instead,
enabling time persistence across reboots.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific configuration]
Signed-off-by: Lukas Rieger <lukas@0x53a.dev>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm660.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm660.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm660.dtsi
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm660.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm660.dtsi
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@
 			compatible = "qcom,qpnp-rtc";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
-			qcom,qpnp-rtc-write = <0>;
+			qcom,qpnp-rtc-write = <1>;
 			qcom,qpnp-rtc-alarm-pwrup = <0>;

 			qcom,pm660_rtc_rw@6000 {
